[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m [response] We are given the following information about Aya's walk:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m - The **distance** of the walk is **9 km**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m - She walks at **constant speed** $ s $ km/h, and the total time (including time in the coffee shop) is **4 hours**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m - When she walks at speed $ s + 2 $ km/h, the total time (including coffee shop) is **2 hours and 24 minutes**, which is **2.4 hours**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m - We are to find the total time in minutes when she walks at speed $ s + \frac{1}{2} $ km/h, **including the $ t $ minutes in the coffee shop**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m ### Step 1: Define variables
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m Let:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m - $ s $ be her walking speed (in km/h)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m - $ t $ be the time spent in the coffee shop (in minutes)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m - She walks **9 km** at speed $ s $, and the **total time** is 4 hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m - So the **walking time** is $ 4 - \frac{t}{60} $ hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m \text{Walking time at speed } s = \frac{9}{s} \text{ hours}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m \frac{9}{s} = 4 - \frac{t}{60} \quad \text{(Equation 1)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m ### Step 2: Use second scenario
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m She walks **at speed $ s + 2 $ km/h**, and total time is 2 hours and 24 minutes = **2.4 hours**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m \text{Walking time at speed } s + 2 = \frac{9}{s + 2} \text{ hours}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} = 2.4 - \frac{t}{60} \quad \text{(Equation 2)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m ### Step 3: Solve system of equations
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m From Equation 1:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m \frac{9}{s} = 4 - \frac{t}{60} \quad \Rightarrow \quad \frac{t}{60} = 4 - \frac{9}{s}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m \quad \Rightarrow \quad t = 60\left(4 - \frac{9}{s} \right) \quad \text{(Equation 1a)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m From Equation 2:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} = 2.4 - \frac{t}{60}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m Now substitute $ t $ from Equation 1a into this:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} = 2.4 - \frac{1}{60} \cdot \left(60\left(4 - \frac{9}{s}\right)\right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} = 2.4 - \left(4 - \frac{9}{s}\right) = 2.4 - 4 + \frac{9}{s} = -1.6 + \frac{9}{s}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m So now we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m \frac{9}{s + 2} = -1.6 + \frac{9}{s} \quad \text{(Equation A)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=122367)[0m $$
